WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.770 line:0%
Welcome back to another episode
of the<i> Wine Down.</i>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.937 line:0%
Woo!
We are pleased

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.572 line:0%
to have our special guest,
Jay Ellis,

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.341
who's famously known
for his character, Lawrence.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.611
Who will be joining us
in unpacking "Lowkey Happy."

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:13.880
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.882
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:16.949 line:0%
ISSA RAE:<i> This was
 a big episode.</i>

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:17.850 line:0%
PRENTICE PENNY:
<i> It was a big episode.</i>

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.585 line:0%
-It went down.
-It went down.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.353
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.892
Issa and Lawrence have been
through a lot this series.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.159
-JAY ELLIS: Mm-hmm.
-Why do you think

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:29.061
this was the right time
for them to unpack

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:30.262
their relationship?

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:33.266 line:0%
It just feels like now
they've both kind

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.001 line:0%
of gotten through that moment,
and can really have

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:37.837
an honest conversation
with each other

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.406
in a way that they never
have before.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:42.408
Where like there's no blame,
there's no

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.076
"your fault, my fault."
You know what I mean?

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.245
Yeah, I also think
Condola's question helped.

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:48.481
Sometimes you don't think
about the what if,

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:52.284
or-- I think that him
being posed that question...

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.552
-ELLIS: Yeah.
-...forced him

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:55.154
to think about things
in a new light.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.757
And the bravery
to have him call her

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:58.892
and try to discuss it
with her,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.826
to see what's up. "What did--
Where did I go wrong?"

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.994
Or, "Did I give up too easily?"

00:01:02.494 --> 00:01:04.730
You know, women can usually--
like, will forgive more,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.499
in a certain way.
We talked about in the room,

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.768 line:0%
of like the reverse of that,
men having a harder time

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:09.936 line:0%
with a woman who cheats
on them,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.937 line:0%
and you want
to unpack that for Lawrence.

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:14.473
And is it just gonna be my pride
that gets in the way of this?

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.510
Or what did I do wrong
to contribute to that?

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.612
Then maybe let me unpack it,
and maybe my feelings

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.946
aren't fully over.

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:22.449
Nothing,
he did absolutely nothing.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.916
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.085
-He did nothing to contribute.
-Wow.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.588
There were lines that you said
in the episode

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:31.524
-that say differently, so...
-Y'all wrote it, so...

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.959
Oh, so you have to say it?
So you don't believe--

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.861
Great acting, son.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:39.232
So the sit-down dinner scene,
what do you think they realize

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.834
about each other,
after having that discussion?

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:45.170
Well there's so many new truths.
I mean, for Issa

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:49.008
to find out that Lawrence
was so deep in doubt

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.910
and insecurities,
and depression,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.511
that he wanted to leave
and go home,

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:54.146
and he was kind of staying
because he didn't want

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:56.716
to let her down.
You know, I think she thinks

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.418
that she was supportive,
but didn't know how

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.319
-to be supportive.
-I think, for me,

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:02.855
it's that dagger moment,
when Issa says,

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.357
that sometimes she used
to just drive around

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:06.959
because she didn't want
to come home.

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.961
Oh, man,
that was heartbreaking.

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.229
Don't nobody ever want
to hear that.

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.431
-Hmm.
-Like processing hearing that

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:15.268
for the first time.
For me, it's this moment

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:18.137
where Lawrence goes, like,
"Oh, shit, I put up this wall."

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.373
-PENNY: Yeah.
-That was so big.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.640
PENNY: Yeah.
What I liked about this

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.843
was it was sharing things
about each other

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.712
that neither the other knew.
"Maybe I bought a ring,"

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.781
"I used to drive around."
Like, "I wanted to move home,

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:30.183
but I didn't tell you."
You know what I mean?

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.317
Like all these types
of things,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.985
of like, "I didn't feel
like you wanted to touch me."

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.286
Like there's so much there
that's like,

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.456
"Oh, we were holding
all this in,

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.157
that maybe had we shared
some of these things--"

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.425
Like why you say,
"Why didn't you tell me?"

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:40.459
It's like, it's hard
to say those things.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:42.395
I mean, you both could've said
those things to each other.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.662
That was
the biggest realization

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:45.999
is that they weren't talking,
you know?

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.335
Condola was like a little mad
in this episode, to me, um...

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.703
She just kept on...

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.605
-...appearing, yeah.
-(MIMICS WHISPERING)

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.974
It's just like,
you know every single time

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:57.143
we got deeper and deeper,
here she comes.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.311
What do you think about
the way that Lawrence

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.148
was responding
to Condola's texts and calls?

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.550
Uh, it reminds me
of those moments

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.518
where it's like,
you're trying

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.455
to do the right thing,
or the thing that feels,

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:10.990
at least, good in the moment.
But, like,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.992
-something kind of keeps, like--
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.260
It's like that Michael Corleone
line,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.361
it's like as soon
as you get out,

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.396
they pull you right back in.
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.198
Like it almost reminded me
of that.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.166
But I think, for him,
I think it was a reminder

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.902
that like, A,
there was something

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.336
that needed to be finished
there.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.738
But, then, B, also,
he was not going to let

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.341
the conversations,
and the texts from Condola

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.577
stop the moment
that he was having with Issa.

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.379
'Cause he, A, may never
get this moment again.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:38.284
And, B, this is the first time
that the two of them

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.387
have been in a space
where they could be vulnerable.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.056
But also be, just kind of,
carefree with each other

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:45.324
and just be relaxed around
each other.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:48.727
I mean that moment,
Lawrence was gonna let Issa go.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.463
Issa, having to, at the end,
kind of step up

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:53.433
and decide, like,
"We're never gonna get

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.701
this moment again.
If I walk out this door,

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.371
I will not be a part
of his tomorrow, Condola might.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:01.440
He might go over there
and rekindle something,

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.911
so this is my only chance."
I say that as soon as Lawrence

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:09.482
invited Issa into the apartment,
and asked to go to the bathroom,

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:12.251
I for sure think that Issa
went in the mirror.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.553
-And had a rap?
-And had a rap.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.956
That was for sure
what she did.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.191
-What about that couch?
-It feels to me like, uh,

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:20.926
when you got a real one,
don't let 'em go.

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.695
-(CHUCKLES)
-That's how it feel to you?

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.797
Yeah, Lawrence hot.
I'm just saying.

00:04:25.497 --> 00:04:27.099
You slipped it,
you thought it was--

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.468
-You thought it was--
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.702
That was about yourself.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.271
So obviously, um, at the end
of the night,

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:35.207
-y'all do the nasty.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.910
I remember in the script
it says, "Make L.O.V.E."

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.345
(ELLIS LAUGHING)

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:43.582
Um... But is there hope
for Issa and Lawrence?

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:47.153
At the end of this episode,
to me, what we see,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.122
is like two people
who are fully accepting

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:51.824
-of each other for who they are.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.460
And Issa-- Issa walking home
at the end of the episode,

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:57.362
kind of just satisfied
with what happened.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:00.466
And I think that satisfaction
goes either way.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:04.003
Like I can walk away from him
and feel like, "Okay,

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.404
I got all the answers
I needed."

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:08.574
Or, "I'm ready to explore
something down the line."

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:11.010
So, we gotta watch and see
which one it is.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.246
Yeah, right?
So thank you again

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.580
for joining us
for another episode

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.382
of the<i> Wine Down.</i>
We can't wait for you

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.650
-to join us again next week.
-ISSA: Woo!

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.218
-Cheers, y'all.
-Two more!

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:20.686
Cheers! Two more episodes!

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.154
-What's gonna happen?
-I don't know.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:25.991
-Well, we know, but...
-(ALL LAUGHING)

